 are an independent risk factor in patients with glaucoma</article-title><source>J Glaucoma</source><volume>9</volume><fpage>134</fpage><lpage>42</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10782622</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b8-opth-1-11"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Atkinson</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Stewart</surname><given-names>WC</given-names></name><name><surname>Fain</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>A new measure of patient satisfaction with ocular hypotensive medications: The Treatment Satisfaction Survey for Intraocular Pressure (TSS-IOP)</article-title><source>Health Qual Life Outcomes</source><volume>1</volume><fpage>67</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14617372</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b9-opth-1-11"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ayyala</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name><name><surname>Cruz</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Margo</surname><given-names>CE</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Cystoid macular edema associated with latanoprost in aphakic and pseudophakic eyes</article-title><source>Am J Ophthalmol</source><volume>126</volume><fpage>602</fpage><lpage>4</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9780112</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b10-opth-1-11"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Barnebey</surname><given-names>HS</given-names></name><name><surname>Orengo-Nania</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Flowers</surname><given-names>BE</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>The safety and efficacy of travoprost 0.004%/timolol 0.5% fixed combination ophthalmic solution</article-title><source>Am J Ophthalmol</source><volume>140</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15990081</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b11-opth-1-11"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Boden</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Sit</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Weinreb</surname><given-names>RN</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Accuracy of an electronic monitoring and reminder device for use with travoprost eye drops</article-title><source>J Glaucoma</source><volume>15</volume><fpage>30</fpage><lpage>4</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16378015</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b12-opth-1-11"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Callanan</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Fellman</surname><given-names>RL</given-names></name><name><surname>Savage</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Latanoprost-associated cystoid macular edema</article-title><source>Am J Ophthalmol</source><volume>126</volume><fpage>134</fpage><lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9683162</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b13-opth-1-11"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cantor</surname><given-names>LB</given-names></name><name><surname>Hoop</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Morgan</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Intraocular pressure-lowering efficacy of bimatoprost 0.03% and travoprost 0.004% in patients with glaucoma or ocular hypertension</article-title><source>Br J Ophthalmol</source><volume>90</volume><fpage>1370</fpage><lpage>3</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16825272</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b14-opth-1-11"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cantor</surname><given-names>LB</given-names></name><name><surname>WuDunn</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Cortes</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Ocular hypotensive efficacy of bimatoprost 0.03% and travoprost 0.004% in patients with glaucoma or ocular hypertension</article-title><source>Surv Ophthalmol</source><volume>49</volume><issue>Suppl 1</issue><fpage>S12</fpage><lpage>S18</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15016557</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b15-opth-1-11"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Carrillo</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name><name><surname>Nicolela</surname><given-names>MT</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Cystoid macular edema in a low-risk patient after switching from latanoprost to bimatoprost</article-title><source>Am J Ophthalmol</source><volume>137</volume><fpage>966</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15126179</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b16-opth-1-11"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cellini</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Caramazza</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Bonsanto</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Prostaglandin analogs and blood-aqueous barrier integrity: a flare cell meter study</article-title><source>Ophthalmologica</source><volume>218</volume><fpage>312</fpage><lpage>17</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15334011</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b17-opth-1-11"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Collaborative Normal-Tension Glaucoma Study Group</collab></person-group><year>19